firm a genuine time-respecting cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion**\n\nStatic reachability from 1010 to 883 clearly exists (e.g. 1010\u2192158\u2192704\u2192883, or 1010\u2192189\u2192704\u2192883), but every tool available reports only whole-horizon aggregates: no timestamps, no per-event times, no window-restricted queries. I therefore cannot verify (a) that any of these edges fired inside [51317, 89717], (b) that they fired in increasing time order, or (c) that consecutive hops are \u2264600 apart. The confounder checks reinforce caution: hub 158 is by far the busiest node in the graph (1029 events, 626 partners \u2014 step_11/step_14), so a static path through it is essentially guaranteed by volume alone and is not evidence of a cascade.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_20982933\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883, 158, 189, 1736, 704],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1010 has only 6 events and 3 out-neighbours (158, 189, 1736); 883 has 8 in-neighbours, of which 704 is reachable in one hop from both 158 and 189, giving static paths 1010->158->704->883 and 1010->189->704->883 (each hop a single or few events). However, no available tool exposes event timestamps or supports restricting to [51317, 89717], so the ordering and the <=600-unit inter-hop delay constraints cannot be tested. Moreover, the candidate relay 158 is the single most active node in the graph (1029 events, 626 partners), so the static path is well explained by hub volume alone. Evidence is therefore insufficient to affirm a genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 36653, "total_output_tokens": 3873, "total_tokens": 40526, "total_latency_ms": 60026, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}